# Build products, generated tables and OS junk.
#
# READ THE ORDERING BEFORE EDITING. This file uses a whitelist in the middle
# (`**/*`, `!**/`, `!**/*.*`) which re-includes every filename containing a dot.
# Anything that must stay ignored despite having a dot in its name has to come
# AFTER that block, because later rules win. That is why several categories
# appear twice: once as intent, once as a final override. Adding a rule above
# the whitelist that matches a dotted filename does nothing.

# Editor/agent workspace state (machine-specific, not project source)
/.claude/
/.worktrees/
.devcontainer/

# Lean/Lake build cache and vendored package checkouts (generated; huge/noisy)
.lake/
/.lake/
# Toolchain clones that concurrent build sessions drop in the tree
/mathlib/

# Scratch and ad-hoc investigation output
/.tmp_find.lean
/diff.txt
/report.md
/build.log
gh_*/
t.py

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# The whitelist. Files with no dot in their name are ignored; directories and
# dotted filenames are re-included. Everything below this block is an override.
**/*
!**/
!**/*.*

# --- Final overrides. Later rules win; these all match dotted names. --------

# Python bytecode caches
**/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/**
*.pyc

# macOS Finder metadata and AppleDouble resource forks
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
._*
**/._*

# Generated extraction tables. Produced from Descent/, which changes
# constantly; a committed snapshot drifts by six figures and reads as
# authoritative while being wrong. Regenerate per worktree -- each producer
# names its command in its own header.
validation/empirical/extract/lean_defs.py
validation/empirical/extract/defs.json
validation/empirical/extract/classes.json
validation/empirical/extract/ceiling.json
validation/empirical/extract/regime.json
validation/empirical/extract/reconcile.json
validation/empirical/extract/coverage.json

# Per-run validator output. These files are regenerated from the current Lean
# sources and must not masquerade as versioned evidence from an older revision.
validation/empirical/differential/results.json
validation/empirical/drift_diff/results_migration_mean.json
validation/empirical/invariants/defs.json
validation/empirical/invariants/results_ranges.json

# The simcov declaration inventory. `validation/empirical/simcov/inventory.py`
# writes it to the current directory, so a run from the repo root drops a copy
# here. It is a 1.9MB snapshot of every declaration in Descent/, regenerated by
# `python3 validation/empirical/simcov/inventory.py` -- same reason as the
# extraction tables above: committed, it drifts and reads as authoritative.
/inventory.json
